The mapper changes build, but the new diagnostic can misclassify non-pressure-assisted accepted choices as pressure-agreement witnesses. The AutoEDA iteration metadata is also left incomplete for stmap73.

Full review comments:

- [P2] Gate accepted witnesses on a real pressure class — /Users/cunxiy/Documents/research/autoresearch-eda/abc-harness/src/map/mapper/mapperMatch.c:4031-4033
  When mode 57 accepts a choice through an existing non-pressure path such as `fProfileOpen` or `Map_MatchNodeHasStmap20EarlySeedDepth`, `!fStrictFallback` can be true while all stmap56 pressure-class flags are false. This block then leaves the source class as `pressure-agreement` and records the row whenever either pressure ratio is at least 1, so the stmap73 diagnostic can report `pressure-agreement` sources with `pressure-agreement = 0` for choices that were not actually pressure-assisted.

- [P2] Finalize the stmap73 iteration state — /Users/cunxiy/Documents/research/autoresearch-eda/abc-harness/.autoeda/runtime/campaign_state.json:9-13
  The tree now contains the stmap73 implementation and generated stmap73 results, but the campaign state still marks iteration 73 as active/prepared with `last_completed_version` left at stmap72, and there is no matching `version73 / stmap73` entry in `versions.md`. Under the recorded correctness contract, this leaves the iteration uncounted and non-reproducible by the campaign tooling.
